  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="tos-no-unfair-advantage">No Unfair Advantage</h2>
    <p>
      TornManager is designed to enhance gameplay by providing data visualization, progress tracking, and 
      tactical information during ranked wars. It does not:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Automate gameplay actions (no auto-attacking, auto-healing, or similar automation)</li>
      <li>Violate Torn's fair play policies</li>
      <li>Offer features that bypass game mechanics</li>
      <li>Perform any actions on your Torn account</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The war features display real-time data sourced from the Torn API (enemy status, hospital timers, 
      online activity) and publicly available spy data. This is the same data available to any player through 
      the Torn API or public spy services — TornManager simply presents it in a more accessible format. 
      I comply with Torn's guidelines on maintaining fair gameplay.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="tos-subscription">Subscription Model</h2>
    <p>
      TornManager uses an in-game subscription model. Access to certain features requires an active subscription, 
      which can be obtained through:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Trial Subscription:</strong> When a faction is first set up on TornManager, all current faction members receive a 1-month trial subscription. This allows the entire faction to explore TornManager's features before committing to a subscription.</li>
      <li><strong>Xanax Payment:</strong> Send Xanax to <%= link_to "Bram [2728237]", "https://www.torn.com/profiles.php?XID=2728237", target: "_blank" %>. Each Xanax sent equals 2 weeks of subscription. Payments are automatically processed daily at 4 AM TCT.</li>
      <li><strong>Subscription Sharing:</strong> Faction leaders with active subscriptions can share subscription weeks with their faction members through the faction settings. This allows leaders to extend access to their members without individual payments.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Subscription status is tied to your Torn ID, not your stored data. If you delete your collected data, 
      your subscription time will be preserved and available when you log back in.
    </p>
  </section>


  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="tos-chats">TornManager Chats (Browser Userscript)</h2>
    <p>
      TornManager Chats is a companion userscript that runs on Torn.com via a userscript manager (such as
      Tampermonkey) and lets you create chat rooms &mdash; and share images &mdash; with other players, beyond the
      faction, company, and private chats Torn provides. Chat rooms are free for every TornManager account and do
      not require a subscription; a Torn API key with Public access level is sufficient to sign in.
    </p>
    <p>By installing and using the chats userscript, you agree to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Allow the userscript to display chat windows on Torn.com pages in your browser</li>
      <li>Allow the userscript to communicate with tornmanager.com to send and receive chat messages and images</li>
      <li>Allow the userscript to store authentication data, encryption keys, and interface preferences in your browser's localStorage</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Private rooms are joined through invite links and are end-to-end encrypted: the invite link carries the
      room's encryption key, which stays in your browser and is never sent to my server. Anyone who has a room's
      invite link can both join the room and read its messages &mdash; treat invite links as secret and only share
      them with people you want in the room. TornManager also hosts public rooms that anyone can join, where you
      appear under a permanent anonymous pseudonym instead of your Torn name; public rooms are not encrypted.
    </p>

    <h3>Acceptable Use</h3>
    <p>
      You alone are responsible for everything you send through the chat feature, including any images you upload.
      You must not use chat rooms to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>harass, threaten, defame, or abuse anyone;</li>
      <li>share content that is illegal under applicable law &mdash; this includes, without limitation, child sexual abuse material (CSAM), which will be removed, preserved, and reported to the relevant authorities;</li>
      <li>upload malware, run scams, or attempt to phish other users;</li>
      <li>violate Torn's rules or Terms of Service; or</li>
      <li>spam, flood, or otherwise disrupt the service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Moderation, Suspension &amp; Bans</h3>
    <p>
      The host of a private room can <strong>suspend</strong> and un-suspend members of that room; a suspended
      member keeps their membership but can no longer read or send messages there.
    </p>
    <p>
      Separately from, and in addition to, the Account Termination terms below, <strong>I reserve the right to ban
      you &mdash; to remove your access to the chat feature, or to TornManager entirely &mdash; at my sole discretion
      and without prior notice if you abuse the extension</strong> or break the Acceptable Use rules above. I may
      also delete individual messages, images, or entire rooms. Where content is unlawful I may preserve it and
      report it, together with the information needed to identify the account responsible, to law enforcement.
    </p>
    <p>
      To keep the service healthy, message and image sending is rate limited, images are limited to PNG or JPG files
      up to a few megabytes each, rooms have a member cap, and each account can be in a limited number of rooms at a
      time.
    </p>
    <p>
      The userscript uses <code>GM.xmlHttpRequest</code> to communicate with tornmanager.com, which bypasses
      standard browser cross-origin restrictions. This is a standard capability of userscript managers and is
      required for the userscript to function. The userscript communicates only with tornmanager.com and torn.com;
      uploaded images are stored with Amazon Web Services (AWS S3, EU region) acting as a processor on my behalf.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="tos-faction-features">Faction Features</h2>
    <p>
      TornManager offers enhanced features for faction leaders and members of tracked factions:
    </p>
    
    <h3>Faction Setup</h3>
    <p>
      When a faction is set up, TornManager uses the provided API key to fetch faction member data. Leaders 
      and Co-leaders are automatically granted access to the Leadership dashboard. All faction members receive 
      a 1-month trial subscription. The faction API key is used to backfill historical personal statistics for 
      all members from the tracking start date.
    </p>

    <h3>Faction API Keys</h3>
    <p>
      Faction leaders may optionally provide a separate faction API key to enable enhanced faction features. 
      By providing a faction API key, you confirm that you are authorized to use that key for faction management 
      purposes and accept responsibility for its use within TornManager.
    </p>
    
    <h3>Faction Whitelists</h3>
    <p>
      Faction leaders can configure whitelists to allow members of other factions to view their faction's training 
      compliance data. By whitelisting another faction, you grant their members read-only access to your faction's 
      aggregate training statistics. You can revoke whitelist access at any time.
    </p>
    
    <h3>Live War Features</h3>
    <p>
      During ranked wars, TornManager provides live war dashboards displaying enemy faction member status, 
      hospital timers, and spy data sourced from public APIs (TornStats). This information is intended to 
      assist with tactical decision-making during wars. The accuracy of spy data depends on third-party sources 
      and may not reflect current battle stats.
    </p>
    <h3>Faction Data Deletion</h3>
    <p>
      Faction leaders can permanently delete all collected faction data through the Leadership dashboard. This 
      removes all personal stat snapshots for faction members, spy reports, ranked war history, API keys, and the 
      leadership whitelist. It also cancels all scheduled background jobs for the faction. Subscription time is 
      preserved for all members. The faction can be set up again at any time. See the 
      <a href="#pp-data-retention">Privacy Policy</a> for the full list of data removed.
    </p>
  </section>

